Fixed in `test/cli/chatgpt_oauth_server_test.dart`.

The second-leg comment no longer claims the leg proves list-order precedence. It now states exactly what the negative assertion covers:

```dart
// The always-available port-0 candidate binds while the held port
// stays occupied. This is a negative-only check: it proves the
// server skips an occupied listed port, but not that it honors
// list order — a positive order assertion would need the
// freed-port TOCTOU probe this fix removes.
```

`dart test test/cli/chatgpt_oauth_server_test.dart` — 14/14 PASSED; `dart analyze` clean.

Fixed in `test/cli/chatgpt_oauth_server_test.dart`.

Both `ChatGptOAuthLocalCallbackServer` instances are now registered with `addTearDown` immediately after construction, so they are closed even when an `expect`/`_httpGet` throws — no more lingering listeners waiting for the 5-second timeout timer in a failed run:

```dart
final fallbackServer = ChatGptOAuthLocalCallbackServer();
addTearDown(fallbackServer.close);
...
final firstServer = ChatGptOAuthLocalCallbackServer();
addTearDown(firstServer.close);
```

`close()` is idempotent (cancels the timer, nulls `_server`), so the happy-path `await server.close()` plus the tearDown close is safe.

`dart test test/cli/chatgpt_oauth_server_test.dart` — 14/14 PASSED; `dart analyze` clean.

